<Legal alt='/es/privacidad' title={'Privacy Policy'} eyebrow='Legal' meta='Last updated: October 11, 2026' lede='What Albena and albena.ai collect, how it is used, and the choices you have.' description='Albena Privacy Policy: no marketing-site cookies or trackers, strictly necessary portal cookies only, local-first processing, no selling data.' toc={toc}>
<section id="summary"><h2>1. Summary</h2><p>Albena is built to be private by default. The marketing site sets no cookies of its own and has no trackers; the customer portal uses only strictly necessary session cookies (see <a href="#cookies">Cookies</a>). On the website we collect only what you submit in a form, such as a waitlist email. Albena processes your information locally first, we never sell it, and we never use it for advertising. You can ask us to delete your data at any time.</p></section>
<section id="website"><h2>2. What this website collects</h2><p>The albena.ai marketing site sets <strong>no cookies of its own and runs no analytics or advertising trackers</strong>. If you join the waitlist we collect the email address you submit; if you contact support we collect the name, email, topic and message you write. Both forms use Cloudflare Turnstile, a privacy-focused verification check that blocks automated spam; it loads only when you reach a form and is subject to Cloudflare&rsquo;s own privacy policy. We use it to manage the waitlist, send early-access invitations and updates about Albena, and answer your messages. You can unsubscribe at any time. Our hosting provider may keep standard server logs (such as IP address and request time) for security and operations.</p></section>
<section id="albena"><h2>3. What Albena processes</h2><p>When you use Albena, depending on what you turn on, she may process:</p><ul><li><strong>Voice:</strong> audio after the wake phrase &ldquo;Hey Albena,&rdquo; and transcripts of your requests.</li><li><strong>Home and devices:</strong> device names, states and commands for smart-home products you connect.</li><li><strong>Calendar and mail:</strong> events, messages and drafts, only if you connect those accounts.</li><li><strong>Memory:</strong> preferences and facts you ask Albena to remember.</li></ul><p>You decide what to connect, and you can disconnect it at any time.</p></section>
<section id="local"><h2>4. Local-first processing</h2><p>Albena runs on hardware in your home wherever possible, so audio, device data and memory are processed there first. When a request needs a more capable cloud AI model, only the information needed for that request is sent, to a provider acting on our behalf, and you will be told what leaves your home. Connected services such as email or calendar providers handle your data under their own policies.</p></section>
<section id="use"><h2>5. How we use information</h2><p>We use information to provide and improve Albena, secure the Services, communicate with you, and meet legal obligations. We do <strong>not</strong> sell your personal information or share it for cross-context behavioral advertising, and we do not use your voice, home, calendar or mail data for advertising or to train general AI models.</p></section>
<section id="sharing"><h2>6. Who we share it with</h2><p>We share information only with service providers that help us run the Services (such as website hosting and email delivery) under confidentiality obligations (see our <a href="/subprocessors">subprocessors page</a>), with cloud AI providers as described above, when you direct us to, or when required by law or to protect rights and safety. We do not sell data. Authorized Albena staff may view your account, Hub and billing status read-only to provide support; every such view is logged.</p><p>Your Hub&rsquo;s current public IP address and approximate location (derived by our network provider) are shown to the account owner and to authorized support staff to troubleshoot connectivity; we keep only the current value.</p></section>
<section id="cookies"><h2>Cookies and similar technologies</h2><p><strong>Marketing site (albena.ai).</strong> We do not set cookies on the marketing site, and we use no analytics, advertising or tracking cookies or pixels. Our network provider may use strictly necessary security checks (for example Cloudflare Turnstile on the forms) to block automated abuse.</p><p><strong>Customer portal (account.albena.ai).</strong> After you sign in, the portal sets a small number of <strong>strictly necessary</strong> first-party cookies. They are all <code>HttpOnly</code>, <code>Secure</code> and scoped to the portal only:</p><ul><li><strong>Session cookie</strong> keeps you signed in. It lasts up to 7 days, ends sooner if you sign out or are idle for 12 hours, and is deleted when you sign out.</li><li><strong>Sign-in verification cookies</strong> tie a one-time email link or passkey ceremony to the browser that requested it. They last 5 to 15 minutes.</li><li><strong>Support view cookie</strong> is used only by authorized Albena staff, for up to 30 minutes, when they view an account read-only to help you. Customers never receive it.</li></ul><p>The sign-in page may also keep the email address you typed in your browser&rsquo;s session storage for that tab only, so the next sign-in step can show it; it is cleared when you close the tab. We do not use these for tracking or advertising.</p><p><strong>No cookie banner.</strong> Strictly necessary cookies that are needed to provide a service you asked for do not require consent under the rules that apply to us, so we do not show a cookie banner or a cookie preferences dialog. If we ever add a non-essential cookie we will ask first and update this section.</p></section>
<section id="gpc"><h2>Global Privacy Control</h2><p>We do not sell or share personal information for cross-context behavioral advertising and the site has no advertising trackers, so there is nothing for an opt-out signal to switch off. We nonetheless treat a browser-sent <a href="https://globalprivacycontrol.org/" rel="noopener">Global Privacy Control</a> (GPC) signal as a valid request to opt out of sale and sharing, and it is honored automatically as no such sale or sharing takes place. <em>Draft pending counsel review.</em></p></section>
<section id="retention"><h2>7. Retention and deletion</h2><p>We keep waitlist emails until you unsubscribe or ask us to delete them, or until early access ends. Data stored by Albena in your home stays under your control and can be removed in the app. To delete data we hold, email us and we will complete the request within 30 days, except where we must keep limited records by law.</p></section>
<section id="children"><h2>8. Children</h2><p>The Services are not directed to children under 13, and we do not knowingly collect their personal information. If you believe a child has given us information, email us and we will delete it. Parents and guardians who use Albena in a household are responsible for the people and devices they connect.</p></section>
<section id="security"><h2>9. Security</h2><p>We use reasonable technical and organizational safeguards, including encryption in transit, access controls and local-first design to limit what leaves your home. No system is perfectly secure, so we cannot guarantee absolute security. Please keep your devices and accounts protected.</p></section>
<section id="rights"><h2>10. Your rights</h2><p>Depending on where you live (for example California under the CCPA/CPRA, or the EEA and UK under the GDPR), you may have the right to access, correct, delete or export your personal information, to object to or restrict certain processing, to withdraw consent, and to not be discriminated against for exercising your rights. We do not sell or share personal information for advertising. To make a request, email <a href="mailto:privacy@albena.ai">privacy@albena.ai</a>. See <a href="#states">US state privacy rights</a> for how to appeal. We may need to verify your identity, and you may complain to your local data protection authority.</p></section>
<section id="states"><h2>US state privacy rights <span class="draft-tag">(draft pending counsel)</span></h2><p><em>This section is a working draft that has not yet been reviewed by legal counsel. It may change, and it does not create rights or obligations beyond those the law gives you.</em></p><p>Residents of California, Colorado, Connecticut, Virginia, Texas, Oregon and other US states with comprehensive privacy laws may have the following rights, depending on the state and on whether the law applies to us:</p><ul><li><strong>Know and access</strong> the personal information we hold about you and the categories of sources and recipients.</li><li><strong>Correct</strong> inaccurate information and <strong>delete</strong> information we hold.</li><li><strong>Portability:</strong> receive your information in a portable format.</li><li><strong>Opt out</strong> of the sale of personal information, of sharing for cross-context behavioral advertising (California), and of targeted advertising or certain profiling. We do none of these things.</li><li><strong>Limit use of sensitive personal information</strong> (California). We use sensitive information, such as precise account or household data you give us, only to provide the service.</li><li><strong>Non-discrimination</strong> for exercising your rights.</li></ul><p><strong>How to make a request.</strong> Email <a href="mailto:privacy@albena.ai">privacy@albena.ai</a> from the address on your account, or use the form on our <a href="/support">support page</a>. We confirm receipt within 10 business days and respond within 45 days, and we may extend once by another 45 days where the law allows and we tell you why. We may need to verify your identity, and you may use an authorized agent.</p><p><strong>Appeals.</strong> If we decline all or part of a request, reply to our response, or email <a href="mailto:privacy@albena.ai?subject=Privacy%20appeal">privacy@albena.ai</a> with the subject &ldquo;Privacy appeal&rdquo; and your reasons. We will respond to the appeal in writing within 45 days (Colorado, Connecticut, Virginia and Texas: 60 days where the law gives us that long), explain the outcome, and tell you how to contact your state attorney general or privacy regulator if you disagree.</p><p><strong>Categories.</strong> In the last 12 months we have collected: identifiers and contact details (name, email) from the waitlist, account and support forms; account and household settings you give the portal; and standard connection data (IP address, request time) in server logs. We have not sold or shared personal information, and we have not disclosed it except to service providers that help us run the service (see <a href="/subprocessors">subprocessors</a>).</p></section>
<section id="changes"><h2>11. Changes to this policy</h2><p>We may update this policy as Albena evolves. We will change the date above and, for material changes, notify waitlist and early-access members by email.</p></section>
<section id="contact"><h2>12. Contact</h2><p>Privacy questions or requests? Email <a href="mailto:privacy@albena.ai">privacy@albena.ai</a>, or see our <a href="/support">support page</a>. Omar Huertas LLC.</p></section>
</Legal>
